prompt:
Use Three.js to implement a 3D product inspection tool. Load the external ScatteringSkull.glb model, support rotational viewing with OrbitControls, and place 4 clickable annotation hotspots (red dots) on the model surface. Clicking a hotspot must open an information panel and highlight the corresponding area.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules within <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/ScatteringSkull.glb;
(2) After loading is complete, center the model at the scene origin and scale it appropriately so that its size is suitable for the viewport;
(3) After loading is complete, set window.__3D_STATE__.modelLoaded = true;

[OrbitControls]
(4) Use OrbitControls to enable orbiting around the model, with rotation, zooming, and panning support;
(5) Set appropriate minimum/maximum zoom distances (minDistance=1, maxDistance=10);

[Annotation Hotspot System]
(6) Preset 4 hotspot positions on the model surface (defined using world coordinates). Represent each hotspot with a small red sphere (SphereGeometry, radius=0.05, red emissive material);
(7) Information for the 4 hotspots:
  - Hotspot 0: position approximately (0.3, 0.3, 0.5), title "Forehead Damage", description "There are obvious impact marks on the forehead area of the helmet";
  - Hotspot 1: position approximately (-0.4, 0.1, 0.3), title "Left-Side Crack", description "A long, thin crack has appeared on the left side of the visor";
  - Hotspot 2: position approximately (0.0, -0.3, 0.5), title "Chin Guard", description "The chin guard is slightly deformed, but its structure remains intact";
  - Hotspot 3: position approximately (0.0, 0.4, -0.3), title "Rear Dent", description "There is a slight dent in the rear area";
(8) Use Raycaster to detect mouse clicks on hotspots;

[Hotspot Interaction]
(9) After a hotspot is clicked:
  a) That hotspot changes to glowing yellow (set emissive to yellow 0xffff00), while the other hotspots return to red;
  b) Display the hotspot title and description in a fixed panel on the right side of the page (id="infoPanel");
  c) Update __3D_STATE__.selectedHotspot to the hotspot index (0-3);
(10) Clicking an empty area cancels the selection, sets selectedHotspot to -1, and hides infoPanel;

[HUD Display]
(11) The HUD in the upper-left corner displays:
  - Selected hotspot number (id="selectedId", displaying 0-3 or "None");
  - Model loading status (id="loadStatus");
  - Total number of hotspots (id="hotspotCount");

[Visual Effects]
(12) Use a dark gray background (0x222222) for the scene;
(13) Add DirectionalLight + AmbientLight + an optional EnvironmentMap to enhance the metallic appearance;

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
  - modelLoaded: boolean (whether the model has finished loading)
  - selectedHotspot: number (currently selected hotspot index 0-3, or -1 when none is selected)
  - hotspotCount: number (total number of hotspots, which should be 4)
  - cameraDistance: number (distance from the camera to the origin)
  - hotspotPositions: Array<{x,y,z}> (world coordinates of the 4 hotspots)
  - highlightActive: boolean (whether any hotspot is currently highlighted)

Output a single HTML file. Place this file in the same directory as the assets/ folder and run it through a local HTTP server.
